  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "block_id": "h1-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Mission Context DuckDB Design",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This design keeps DuckDB in the role of a rebuildable analytical index, not a canonical governance store.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "What DuckDB Is For",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Indexing canonical docs, schemas, audits, receipts, and optional work ledger files. - Running deterministic queries to locate relevant packet sources. - Producing typed packet components from explicit allow-listed roots.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "What DuckDB Is Not For",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- It is not the source of truth. - It is not a shared mutable ledger. - It is not a daemon. - It is not the packet format.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Rebuildability Rule",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If the cache disappears, the compiler must be able to rebuild it from canonical files.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Compilation Rule",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Packet compilation should:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- read from explicit source paths only, - remain deterministic, - preserve ordering where the schema requires it, - reject raw content fields, - emit a content-light receipt.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The prototype compiler may operate directly on the filesystem first and add DuckDB later without changing the packet contract.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-13",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Likely Helper Boundary",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If a helper is added later, it should:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- open a local cache under `.build/rig/context/`, - ingest from explicit allow-listed roots, - return typed packet components, - avoid ambient filesystem crawling.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-16",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Future Integration",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "DuckDB can later support packet source discovery, but the executable contract is the packet model and receipt schema first.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    }
  ],
